{"id":21070,"name":"Austin County","slug":"austin-county","state":"Texas","code":"TX","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/redeemable-tax-deed/redeemable-tax-deed-states/texas-redeemable-tax-deeds-how-to-join-the-auction/austin-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-02-04T07:21:44","facts":null,"bodyHtml":"\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-austin-county-texas-tax-sales\">How Austin County, Texas, Tax Sales</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Tax sales in Austin County, Texas, are organized to recover unpaid property taxes and are an opportunity for investors to acquire properties. These sales follow a structured process, ensuring that the county recoups lost revenue while giving property owners a chance to resolve their debts.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Understanding the Sale Process</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Tax sales in Austin County are held on the <strong>first Tuesday of each month</strong>. These sales take place at the Austin County Courthouse or a designated location, starting promptly at the scheduled time. Properties sold are those with delinquent taxes that have remained unpaid despite notices sent to the property owner.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-announcements-and-notifications\">Announcements and Notifications</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:post-content -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bidding and Minimum Requirements</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #6b707f; font-size: 16px;\">The minimum bid for a property is the total amount of </span><strong style=\"color: #6b707f; font-size: 16px;\">delinquent taxes, penalties, interest, and associated fees</strong><span style=\"color: #6b707f; font-size: 16px;\">. This amount is announced during the sale.</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The highest bidder who meets or exceeds the minimum bid wins the property</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Buyers typically make payment immediately after the sale. Confirm accepted payment methods and exact deadlines before attending.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:image {\"id\":21072,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":37368,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"align\":\"center\",\"className\":\"wp-block-image size-full\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse.webp\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse.webp 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-541x360.webp 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-296x197.webp 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Austin-County-Courthouse-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-37368 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Austin County Courthouse\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:image --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:buttons {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\">\n<p><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --></p>\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:spacer --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Redemption Period</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:heading --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Texas law allows property owners a redemption period after the sale:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Six months</strong> for non-homestead properties.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Two years</strong> for homestead or agricultural properties.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>During this period, owners can reclaim their property by paying the sale price plus a penalty. The penalty increases over time:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>25% if redeemed in the first year.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>50% if redeemed in the second year (for applicable properties).</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Post-Sale Procedures</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #6b707f; font-size: 16px;\">Buyers are issued a tax deed, which transfers ownership but may not clear all liens.</span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>It is the buyer’s responsibility to address any remaining encumbrances.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Title insurance may be challenging to obtain immediately, and quiet title actions are sometimes necessary to secure a clear title.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preparing for the Sale</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:heading --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Interested buyers should research each property thoroughly. This includes:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Checking for any liens or encumbrances that may remain after purchase.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Visiting the property (if accessible) to assess its condition.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Confirming details with the <strong>Austin County Appraisal District</strong> or consulting a legal expert for clarity on the process.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Reviewing auction rules, which can vary by county and may include specific requirements for registration and bidding.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list-item --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:list --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Useful Links</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #6b707f; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/austin-county-texas-redeemable-deed-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Auction Calendar</a></span></span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/redeemable-tax-deed/redeemable-tax-deed-states/texas-redeemable-tax-deeds-how-to-join-the-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Profit from Texas’s Redeemable Deeds</span></a></span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/redeemable-tax-deed/redeemable-tax-deed-overview/understanding-a-redeemable-tax-deed/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Let&#8217;s talk about redeemable tax deeds and how you can profit from them!</span></a></span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ES5ZPyHRFMM?si=EmzhADUvwB_2FAAr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Discover Tax Deeds and how you can find property for as little as $50! </span></a></span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IQzw3wwWlRs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Learn How to maximize profits at the Texas Tax Sales</span></a></span></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:heading --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading\"} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Need A Hand?</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- /wp:heading --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Start exploring our <span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/general-auction-calendar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Auction Calendar</a></span> to stay informed about upcoming auctions. Mark your calendar for Austin County’s tax sales, and don’t miss your chance to participate! If you’d like more guidance or have specific questions, <span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">book a call</a></span> with an expert to get personalized advice. You can also explore our <span style=\"color: #0693e3;\"><a style=\"color: #0693e3;\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">free resources</a></span> for helpful tips and answers to common questions, ensuring you’re ready to make confident decisions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><p><em>Sign up or log in to view the full content.</em></p><div id=\"popup-overlay\"></div><div id=\"signup-popup\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 20px;\"><h4>Get Instant Free Access To The Training Vault Now</h4><p>Learn how to get 18-36% returns on your investment and buy property for as little as $500 with tax lien and tax deeds.</p><div class=\"video-container\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\"><iframe src=\"https://youtube.com/embed/FkB-M8RaSHo\" allowfullscreen style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 560px; height: 315px; border: none; border-radius: 8px;\"></iframe></div><div class=\"button-container\" style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\"><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Sign Up for FREE Access</button><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Already a Member? Login</button></div></div>","upcomingCount":0}